{# Decision template: how the player meant a line spoken to the dog, as one choice. Sent by Canine Drives for each
   player line addressed to him (he is the line's target, or he is named in it while close by). The plugin acts on
   the choice: praise and scolding move his need for affection, feed hands him food from the player's pack.

   Context set by the plugin: dogFormId, playerName, line (the player's words), telepathy (true when sent over the
   mind-link), hunger (0-100, higher = hungrier). #}
{% set dogUUID = formid_to_uuid(dogFormId) %}
{% set dog = decnpc(dogUUID) %}

[ state dog ]
{{ dog.name }} is a dog, a companion of {{ playerName }}. Hunger {{ hunger }} of 100.
[ end state ]

[ state line ]
{{ playerName }} {% if telepathy %}reached into {{ dog.name }}'s mind and sent{% else %}said to {{ dog.name }}{% endif %}: "{{ line }}"
[ end state ]

[ question meaning choice ]
How did {{ playerName }} mean this line to {{ dog.name }}? Judge the words and their tone, the way an owner talks to a dog. A line often mixes things: when praise, a scolding or an offer of food sits alongside a command, a question or chatter ("Get him! Good boy!"), choose the praise, scolding or food.
[ criteria ]
praise: warm approval or love for him: "good boy", "well done", "that's my brave dog", "I love you, boy", thanks or pride in something he did.
scold: disapproval or a telling-off: "bad dog", "no!", "stop that", "drop it", anger or disappointment at something he did.
call_off: telling him to stop attacking or let someone go: "leave it!", "back off!", "let him go", "enough!", "heel!" in or after a fight. An order to stop fighting is call_off, not scold.
feed: an offer of food to eat now: "here, have this sweetroll", "eat up", "want some meat?", handing him something to eat. Not a promise of food later, and not a toy or a bone to chew.
other: anything else: questions, commands, plans, chatting, talk about other things.
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
